      "title": "Agent Skills Marketplace for AI Code Assistants",
      "why_now": "Explosive growth of agent-skills, claude-code-plugin, and cursor-rules (velocity 2187.57) shows developers are creating custom behaviors but lack a centralized, discoverable, versioned ecosystem to share and reuse these skills. High-severity pain from open-webui indicates users struggle to configure advanced agentic behaviors, pointing to an urgent need for curated, plug-and-play skill packs.",
      "problem": "Developers writing agent skills (prompts, rules, tool integrations) for Claude Code and Cursor work in silos with no standard format, sharing mechanism, or quality control, leading to duplicated effort and inconsistent agent performance.",
